                        ],
                        "form": "cadavéreuse"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c097c55-33d4-417a-87fd-fcd5535586c7",
                        "entry_id": "0c0cb13e-9673-31b8-a963-54d342f82705",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "cadavéreuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                        "entry_id": "0c0cb13e-9673-31b8-a963-54d342f82705",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui tient du cadavre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b4807ea-1f59-40f6-809c-19f2f9fada61",
                                "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                                "text": "— Je le crois bien, pensa encore le fils en s’agenouillant au chevet du lit et en baisant une des mains cadavéreuses de Bartholoméo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb0296c0-6922-4d1c-b18f-7b84048df71c",
                                "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                                "text": "J’y dépeignais les sensations d’un homme conservant sous terre toutes les passions qu’il avait eues dessus, et j’intitulai cette rêverie cadavéreuse : La vie dans la mort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3796f734-1ff7-456d-b70b-e436fab09f42",
                                "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                                "text": "Je ne me souviens pas d’avoir aperçu par la pensée, soit dans les charniers de la Bible, soit dans les scènes les plus fantastiques de notre littérature cadavéreuse, un spectacle aussi épouvantablement majestueux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3289ee1-a3da-4abc-87c8-39adaddd218b",
                                "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                                "text": "Aucun rendez-vous ne s’était passé d’une manière plus décente, ni plus chaste, ni plus froide peut-être, dans un lieu plus horrible par les détails, devant une plus hideuse divinité ; car cette mère était restée dans l’imagination d’Henri comme quelque chose d’infernal, d’accroupi, de cadavéreux, de vicieux, de sauvagement féroce, que la fantaisie des peintres et des poètes n’avait pas encore deviné."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fff3692-434e-4263-9ee0-d2a8b2293fa9",
                                "sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                                "text": "L’expression de désespoir qui se peint sur toutes ces physionomies cadavéreuses, dans ces orbites sans yeux, qui voient que leur labeur a été inutile, est vraiment tragique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9b8854b1-d7d6-46af-b9df-084304dc7d19",
                        "source_entry_id": "0c0cb13e-9673-31b8-a963-54d342f82705",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e083f7d-07b3-31d9-b12f-a0d3f3a20ce8",
                        "target_lang_word": "cadaverous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cadaverous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                        "entry_id": "36cef88e-f22f-3afc-8144-dc0f746c0801",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Corpselike; hinting of death; imitating a cadaver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f2f8d94-9765-4068-af0e-83a95c43fb55",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "The speakers were three men, rather beyond middle life. One was pale and cadaverous, as if every feature gave testimony to the length of his vigils and the rigour of his fasts, while straight black hair hanging down on each side his face added to his wild and neglected appearance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d117f61-a7f2-4250-9481-ac4c67cbf7d8",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "It may have been the sight of that cadaverous ambition and self-complacent meanness, which showed itself in Paley’s yellow face, and twinkled in his narrow eyes, or it may have been a natural appetite for pleasure and joviality, of which it must be confessed Mr. Pen was exceedingly fond, which deterred that luckless youth from pursuing his designs upon the Bench or the Woolsack with the ardour, or rather steadiness, which is requisite in gentlemen who would climb to those seats of honour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c48396fc-fb41-4495-bef5-1a32f2927d35",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "Some approached pure blanching; some had a bluish pallor; some worn by the older characters (which had possibly lain by folded for many a year) inclined to a cadaverous tint, and to a Georgian style."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ceec39f-484a-4fb6-9283-71e0f8b5ae00",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "1917 rev. 1925 Ezra Pound, \"Canto I\"\nDark blood flowed in the fosse,\nSouls out of Erebus, cadaverous dead ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b573a109-76d8-48ac-a921-adead6744151",
                                                "sense_id": "f5f4e1f4-1d86-3656-a9fc-9a2cb00af96f",
                                                "text": "By some paradoxical evolution rancour and intolerance have been established in the vanguard of primitive Christianity. Mrs. Spoker, in common with many of the stricter disciples of righteousness, was as inclement in demeanour as she was cadaverous in aspect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aabe1244-1e1c-4ec4-b88d-f0b23b8fc4b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "0c0cb13e-9673-31b8-a963-54d342f82705",
